==========================================================================
MEDIUM-INDUCED DECOHERENCE: is there any?
==========================================================================

[1] The medium's own scales
    alpha_c = 3*alpha        = 0.0218921
    c_s     = sqrt(alpha_c)  = 0.1479596 c = 44,357 km/s
    xi      = hbar/(m c_s)   = 5.9538e+13 m = 398.0 AU
    mu      = m c_s^2        = 4.9038e-22 eV  ->  5.6906e-18 K

[2] The dispersion, and where the Landau threshold sits
    Bogoliubov:  omega(q) = c_s q sqrt(1 + (q xi / 2)^2)
    The corpus's xi = hbar/(m c_s) IS the Bogoliubov healing length, so the
    dispersion is fixed with no further input. Landau critical velocity is
    v_c = min_q [omega(q)/q]. For this branch omega/q rises monotonically
    from c_s, so the minimum is the q->0 limit:

      q*xi      (omega/q)/c_s
        0.00    1.000000
        0.01    1.000012
        0.10    1.001249
        1.00    1.118034
       10.00    5.099020

    numerical min over q*xi in [0,20]: 1.000000000  (analytic: 1)
    => v_c = c_s = 44,357 km/s = 0.1480 c
    No roton minimum exists on a Bogoliubov branch, so v_c is not reduced.

[3] Mechanism one: nothing in the lab can excite the medium
    Landau threshold: 44,357 km/s

      probe                          v (km/s)     v/v_c     excitable?
      lab apparatus, thermal             1.0   2.25e-05   no
      Earth's orbital motion            29.8   6.72e-04   no
      Sun through the galaxy           220.0   4.96e-03   no
      Earth through the CMB frame      369.8   8.34e-03   no
      fast solar wind                  800.0   1.80e-02   no

    Below v_c there is no final state conserving both energy and momentum,
    so the medium cannot record which path was taken. No record, no decoherence.
    This is exact at T = 0, and it is kinematics, not a small coupling.

[4] Mechanism two: the order parameter cannot resolve a lab superposition
    The condensate varies on scale xi. Two paths separated by dx perturb it by
    a relative amount ~ (dx/xi)^2, which is the decoherence-rate suppression.

    xi = 5.954e+13 m

      superposition                 dx (m)       dx/xi        (dx/xi)^2
      atom interferometer           1.00e-09   1.680e-23    2.821e-46
      large-molecule fringe         1.00e-06   1.680e-20    2.821e-40
      optomechanical mirror         1.00e-03   1.680e-17    2.821e-34
      metre-scale, hypothetical     1.00e+00   1.680e-14    2.821e-28
      Earth-Sun distance            1.50e+11   2.513e-03    6.313e-06

    A micron superposition is suppressed by 3e-40 before any coupling constant
    is applied. The two mechanisms are independent: one kills the rate on
    velocity grounds, the other on length grounds. Both give zero.

[5] The only loophole: finite temperature. It closes itself.
    Thermal phonons are not Landau-forbidden, so a T > 0 medium has a normal
    component that can scatter. The relevant length is the thermal phonon
    wavelength lambda_T = hbar c_s / (k_B T), and the suppression becomes
    (dx/lambda_T)^2 instead of (dx/xi)^2. So the question is whether lambda_T
    can ever fall below xi.

      at T = mu/k_B = 5.691e-18 K :  lambda_T = 5.9538e+13 m
      xi                              =  5.9538e+13 m

    lambda_T = xi exactly at T = mu/k_B. That is not a coincidence: it is the
    same Bogoliubov relation read twice. And T > mu/k_B is the regime where the
    phonon description fails and the condensate itself is destroyed -- the
    medium would no longer be the superfluid the model requires.

    So for any T at which the model's medium exists at all, lambda_T >= xi,
    and the finite-T suppression is WEAKER than the T = 0 one is strong.
    The loophole does not open.
      T = 1.00e-20 K -> lambda_T = 3.388e+16 m  (569.06 xi)   condensed
      T = 1.00e-18 K -> lambda_T = 3.388e+14 m  (  5.69 xi)   condensed
      T = 5.69e-18 K -> lambda_T = 5.954e+13 m  (  1.00 xi)   condensed
      T = 1.00e-16 K -> lambda_T = 3.388e+12 m  (  0.06 xi)   NOT condensed (phonons gone)

[6] Where the threshold is NOT vacuous: relativistic matter
    v_c = 0.1480 c is low. Anything with gamma above a few sits above it.

      particle                       beta       above v_c?
      beta = 0.148 (threshold)     0.147960   no
      1 MeV electron               0.941079   YES
      10 MeV electron              0.998818   YES
      1 GeV proton (KE)            0.875066   YES
      cosmic ray, 1 TeV proton     1.000000   YES

    Every relativistic particle in the universe is supercritical and may emit
    medium phonons by a Cherenkov process. That is a real channel, and it is
    where a bound on the matter-medium coupling has to come from -- not from
    tabletop decoherence, which this calculation has just shown is dead.

==========================================================================
VERDICT
==========================================================================

    The ULTRALIGHT DARK CONDENSATE induces no decoherence of its own on any
    laboratory superposition. (Sector matters: the vacuum is a separate condensate
    whose excitations ride the light cone, so its own Landau velocity is c and
    nothing outruns it -- that is the zero-drag certificate behind inertia, a
    different argument that must not be merged with this one.)

    This is a null with a mechanism -- two mechanisms, independent of each other:

      (a) Landau.    v_c = sqrt(3 alpha) c = 0.1479596 c = 44,357 km/s. Every terrestrial
                     and solar-system velocity is below it by at least two orders of
                     magnitude, so no excitation is kinematically allowed at all.

      (b) Rigidity.  xi = 402 AU. The order parameter cannot resolve a separation
                     smaller than that; a micron superposition is suppressed by
                     (dx/xi)^2 = 3e-40 before any coupling is applied.

    Finite temperature does not rescue the effect: lambda_T >= xi throughout the
    entire range in which the medium remains condensed, with equality exactly at
    T = mu/k_B where the condensate ends.

    WHAT THIS COSTS THE MODEL. It forbids the model from ever claiming credit for
    an anomalous decoherence signal. If a tabletop experiment reports collapse
    beyond the environmental prediction, this medium cannot be its cause. The
    prohibition is forced by the two numbers above and cannot be tuned away
    without giving up either alpha_c = 3 alpha or m = 2.24e-20 eV.

    WHAT IT BUYS. A dark-sector null with thresholds: this ultralight medium cannot
    be blamed for anomalous tabletop decoherence. Foundations seating of QM remains
    interpretation; Born stays open. Do not read this null as "the model provides QM."

    WHERE THE LIVE PHYSICS MOVED. Upward in velocity. v_c = 0.148 c is low enough
    that all relativistic matter is supercritical, so the medium's one open
    decoherence-adjacent channel is Cherenkov phonon emission by fast particles.
    That is the corner worth computing next.

